  "note": "Samuel Sterling, town clerk, received nine nominations for the nine seats, so there was no contest. Robert Caughey, \"a representative of the mill-workers\", took the place of Isaac Barr, who had ceased to be a member some months earlier. T. H. White was the retiring chairman."
